  "what_changed": "One image set for hosts and players. Heltec kart images rebuilt from the merge of upstream through 6e4c788: they report kart-0.3.6 and carry upstream 0.3.4 to 0.3.6 (no WiFi for an empty or sentinel SSID, no driver reconnect loop, `wifi clear`, fixed ESP-NOW channel 1 whenever WiFi is off, a carried SHIELD blocks one multiplayer hit). On a paired M5 kart the Pi inventory is compiled out, so the upstream shield path is a stub there; the M5 player's own shield (armed with FIRE) is unchanged. Core2 images are the 2026-11-13-site-map files, byte for byte. Base and repeater are the 2026-11-13-upstream-035 files, byte for byte: upstream changed neither.",
  "compatibility": "Course package rules version 2. Host Heltec, host Pi server, player Heltec and player Core2 must all be from this source for course download, JOIN and FIRE. The LoRa protocol is unchanged from kart-0.3.3, so pit commands, pit races and telemetry work between this build and older ones. An M5 kart cannot join a ROAM freeplay: ROAM has no course.",
